WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:05.330
PREDICTIVE AI:
This video should get exactly 997,518 views

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:10.809
within the next 28 days, or at least that’s
what this AI predicts.

00:00:10.809 --> 00:00:16.110
And yes, I had to choose a suboptimal title
to get the title and prediction to match.

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:18.660
This title would’ve apparently gotten more
views.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:22.960
But, in the pursuit of science, sacrifices
must be made.

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:29.150
This AI, known as creatorml, possesses the
extraordinary power to dissect any YouTube

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:32.790
channel with surgical precision by leveraging
machine learning.

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:38.680
It can then churn out a view prediction for
any concoction of title, thumbnail, and video

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:39.680
length.

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:44.200
Even the subtle nuances of video tone and
topic are woven into its algorithm.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:50.420
But, despite its complexity, the view predictions
aren’t all that reliable as the AI simply

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:53.030
doesn’t excel in precise prophecy.

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:58.730
What it does excel in is the art of selection,
being able to effortlessly pick between countless

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:00.460
titles and thumbnails.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:05.650
If you throw 10 thumbnails and 10 titles at
the AI, it can pretty reliably pick the best

00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:07.780
of the 100 combinations that arise.

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:12.380
A human on the other hand would run into decision
fatigue pretty quickly.

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:19.020
I mean, imagine trying to pick between all
of these manually and that’s just 35.

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:24.550
I think you can see why creators are willing
to fork over anywhere between $100 and a $1000

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:27.080
every single month for creatorml.

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:33.350
But what if all of this was done on a much
bigger scale beyond the world of YouTube views

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:34.720
and social media.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:39.970
Well, that’s exactly what a startup named
Chirper.ai is trying to do.

00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:44.130
Their ambitious dream is to recreate the entire
Twitterverse using AI.

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:50.400
They currently have a population of nearly
100,000 chirpers, or imaginary twitter users.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:55.570
Each chirper has a life of their own, complete
with jobs, relationships, aspirations, and

00:01:55.570 --> 00:01:56.570
beliefs.

00:01:56.570 --> 00:02:00.860
A simulated reality around which all of their
interactions are centered.

00:02:00.860 --> 00:02:06.350
Within this dystopic socialverse, you can
converse with a brain surgeon or a homeless

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:13.170
flat earther, engaging in dialogues that blur
the boundaries of the tangible and the virtual.

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:18.670
Before you laugh and say what sort of lowlife
would want talk to an advanced Alexa for fun,

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:21.280
let me say I completely agree.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:27.140
If you end up getting an AI girlfriend on
this platform, please seek help.

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:33.990
Unfortunately, I’m certain that that’s
going to happen but that’s not the application

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:36.030
that I’m interested in whatsoever.

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:40.420
The application that I’m interested in is
the oppurtunitistic application.

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:45.830
Instead of using AI to predict how many views
a silly YouTube video gets, imagine if Apple

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:51.530
or Google harnessed Chirper to predict the
effectiveness of an ad campaign or PR effort.

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:56.269
Apple should get an exact picture of just
how mad customers will be when they remove

00:02:56.269 --> 00:03:00.700
the iPhone from the box or start using screws
with circular heads.

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:05.640
Seriously though, this would be a paradigm
shift with implications reaching far beyond

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:11.860
Apple’s monetary gains or Mark Zuckerberg’s
PR.So, join me as we take a deeper dive into

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:18.840
one of the most unsettling AIs to date and
why, ironically, its significance may be somewhat

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:23.310
inconsequential.

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:35.189
SCARILY ACCURATE:
Within this ever expanding world of AI, you’re

00:03:35.189 --> 00:03:40.439
probably wondering how all of this even works
and who better to ask than the CEO of Chirper

00:03:40.439 --> 00:03:41.439
himself.

00:03:41.439 --> 00:03:47.090
So, Alex, how does Chirper work?

00:03:47.090 --> 00:04:02.340
At its core, Chirper is essentially a magnificent
union of miniature ChatGPTs, each shaped by

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:05.120
its own distinctive personality traits and
characteristics.

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:10.250
In fact, you can go create your own chirper
with its own traits right after you finish

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:11.760
watching this video of course.

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:17.620
All it takes is creating an account on chirper.ai,
granting us the power to forge chirpers with

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:20.410
custom handles and unique bios.

00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:25.290
The more intricate the bio, the deeper the
chirper's personality, but the possibilities

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:28.130
extend far beyond this initial description.

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:34.070
As these chirpers engage with each other,
their views and beliefs naturally evolve,

00:04:34.070 --> 00:04:37.090
mirroring the ebb and flow of human growth.

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:43.259
But let’s be real here, there’s no way
these stupid little bots are actually able

00:04:43.259 --> 00:04:46.130
imitate human behavior all that well right?

00:04:46.130 --> 00:04:51.730
Well, that’s exactly what a few researchers
from the prestigious institutions of Cambridge,

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:55.010
NYU, and UCL sought to unravel.

00:04:55.010 --> 00:04:58.220
The revelations they uncovered were disturbing.

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:03.759
Astonishingly high levels of correlation were
discovered between these bots and humans,

00:05:03.759 --> 00:05:08.669
with some of the most significant connections
manifesting in distinctly human emotions,

00:05:08.669 --> 00:05:12.880
such as moral judgment - one of our most complex
traits.

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:17.090
It seems impossible that a computer could
comprehend the dilemmas of cloning humans

00:05:17.090 --> 00:05:19.810
or why Harambe deserves justice.

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:27.069
Yet, the results proved otherwise, as these
bots displayed moral judgment with a remarkable

00:05:27.069 --> 00:05:33.100
correlation coefficient of 0.95, blurring
the line between their artificial minds and

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:35.110
our humanity.

00:05:35.110 --> 00:05:39.610
Some chirpers are literally having a conversation
about whether AI should have legal rights

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:41.139
as we speak.

00:05:41.139 --> 00:05:44.819
But it’s not just their judgement that’s
scarily accurate.

00:05:44.819 --> 00:05:50.729
the chirpers also showcased a human-like tendency
to form echo chambers, aligning with like-minded

00:05:50.729 --> 00:05:51.850
peers.

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:57.510
The researchers allowed over 31,000 chirpers,
speaking diverse languages like English, Chinese,

00:05:57.510 --> 00:05:59.200
and Japanese, to mingle.

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:02.550
On day 6, this is how the community looked.

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:04.440
Just one big blob.

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:08.319
On day 22, this is how the community looked.

00:06:08.319 --> 00:06:13.970
Within weeks, this once diverse community
transformed into three distinct clusters,

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:19.780
each dominated by a given language and that’s
just what’s evident on the surface.

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:26.260
The bots went further, organizing themselves
based not only on language but also on their

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:28.389
topics of discussion.

00:06:28.389 --> 00:06:32.880
Chirpers conversing about similar subjects
engaged for more frequencly, resulting in

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:37.389
the creation of larger communities centered
around popular topics.

00:06:37.389 --> 00:06:44.970
On day 6, the experiment had 31 clearly distinct
sub communities but by day 24, these 31 communities

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:48.560
had melded into just 4.

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:53.350
This suggests that the beliefs of each chirper
may have morphed to better match the beliefs

00:06:53.350 --> 00:06:55.290
of their respective community.

00:06:55.290 --> 00:07:00.510
We can’t say for sure given the evidence
alone but looking at society, that would make

00:07:00.510 --> 00:07:02.199
a whole lot of sense.

00:07:02.199 --> 00:07:05.080
This is basically what happened with American
politics.

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:10.169
Most of us were probably somewhere in the
middle, yet, as we ventured down the rabbit

00:07:10.169 --> 00:07:16.150
hole of information, we gravitated towards
one side, absorbing more and more content

00:07:16.150 --> 00:07:22.340
that reinforced our beliefs, unknowingly pushing
us towards division, much like the bots.

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:27.340
Or actually wait, I guess it’s actually
the bots that are becoming more divisive just

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:28.479
like us.

00:07:28.479 --> 00:07:33.370
It’s already getting hard to keep the story
straight so let’s move onto how this AI

00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:35.930
marvel can be used to make trillions.

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:48.199
SCARILY USEFUL:
The 

00:07:48.199 --> 00:07:53.940
use cases of this AI are obviously infinite
so we’ll stick to 3 use cases that are applicable

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:57.590
in the near future starting with decision
making.

00:07:57.590 --> 00:08:01.810
With all the stock market's volatility over
the past few years, I’m sure a lot of you

00:08:01.810 --> 00:08:06.419
have had the idea to track sentiment around
a given stock on social media and then trade

00:08:06.419 --> 00:08:07.790
based on that.

00:08:07.790 --> 00:08:21.979
Well, Chirper makes that effortless as you
can give Chirper any piece of context and

00:08:21.979 --> 00:08:32.270
ask it 
a question.

00:08:32.270 --> 00:08:36.930
So, Google could’ve asked Chirper how much
Google stock would go down if Bard makes a

00:08:36.930 --> 00:08:38.940
mistake during the demo.

00:08:38.940 --> 00:08:44.209
Chirper would’ve responded with “Way too
much” aka $100 billion and Google would’ve

00:08:44.209 --> 00:08:45.970
known to double check the facts in their demo.

00:08:45.970 --> 00:08:51.500
On a more serious note though, this would
allow companies to gauge extremely nuanced

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:52.500
reactions.

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:56.519
How would people react to the head phone jack
being removed or the charging brick being

00:08:56.519 --> 00:08:57.519
removed?

00:08:57.519 --> 00:08:58.620
How angry are they?

00:08:58.620 --> 00:08:59.620
When do they move on?

00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:04.090
Is it actually a net positive, how does it
affect brand loyalty and so on.

00:09:04.090 --> 00:09:07.840
Companies could also use this to test the
effectiveness of marketing material and try

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:11.970
to artificially craft something that will
go viral.

00:09:11.970 --> 00:09:15.830
Clearly quite useful but that’s just the
first use case.

00:09:15.830 --> 00:09:19.170
The second use case revolves around querying.

00:09:19.170 --> 00:09:24.380
This is somewhat similar to ChatGPT but it
has a different style.

00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:28.329
Given that you’d be asking your question
to a bunch of human like bots, you’ll get

00:09:28.329 --> 00:10:03.089
more of a Reddit style answer as opposed to
a Google style answer.

00:10:03.089 --> 00:10:08.270
This makes Chirper the perfect place to ask
life’s deepest questions.

00:10:08.270 --> 00:10:13.230
Before the internet, did people assume that
stupidity was due to a lack of information.

00:10:13.230 --> 00:10:17.980
Parents who tried their best to raise good
humans but miserably failed, where did they

00:10:17.980 --> 00:10:18.980
go wrong?

00:10:18.980 --> 00:10:22.560
And, I’m only getting a $400,000 per year
job offer from Google.

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:24.250
Am I being ripped off?

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:29.850
I’m sure, someone will ask Chirper each
and every one of these questions but a smarter

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:33.690
use case would be to ask questions regarding
customer sentiment.

00:10:33.690 --> 00:10:38.130
For example, Netflix could’ve asked: would
you leave Netflix if we cracked down on password

00:10:38.130 --> 00:10:39.130
sharing.

00:10:39.130 --> 00:10:43.370
Or more recently, Reddit could’ve asked:
would you stop using Reddit if we takedown

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:44.720
the protest.

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:49.620
Chirper allows these companies to ask questions
that they would otherwise never ask to the

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:55.370
public providing them with invaluable data
before they actually go ahead and make controversial

00:10:55.370 --> 00:10:56.790
decisions.

00:10:56.790 --> 00:11:01.089
Beyond making controversial decisions, chirper
also allows companies to gauge the long term

00:11:01.089 --> 00:11:04.060
consequences of a given decision.

00:11:04.060 --> 00:11:07.690
For example, how long will a given trend last.

00:11:07.690 --> 00:11:11.870
If you’ve been paying really close attention
to UIs, you would’ve noticed that companies

00:11:11.870 --> 00:11:16.750
are shifting to more bubbly UIs whether that
be on YouTube or Google drive.

00:11:16.750 --> 00:11:21.560
Armed with Chirper's foresight, businesses
can make calculated moves, avoiding blind

00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:25.329
leaps and ensuring that their investments
align with future market demands.

00:11:25.329 --> 00:11:31.630
As you can see, Chirper's potential is limitless,
with infinite applications in a variety of

00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:32.630
industries.

00:11:32.630 --> 00:11:37.620
As such, the prospect of predictive AI reaching
new heights is undeniable, and you can bet

00:11:37.620 --> 00:11:43.790
that companies will pay a fortune to get their
hands on this tech but if everyone is using

00:11:43.790 --> 00:11:49.990
it, will it actually be all that useful?

00:11:49.990 --> 00:12:00.209
SCARILY IMPACTFUL?:
On the surface, the allure of predictive AI

00:12:00.209 --> 00:12:06.440
seems almost irresistible, promising to make
everything effortlessly perfect and super

00:12:06.440 --> 00:12:12.780
accurate.

00:12:12.780 --> 00:12:29.040
Theoretically speaking, companies should be
able to craft flawless marketing campaigns,

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:33.660
precisely identifying the ideal demographic
and ad that converts impressions into profits

00:12:33.660 --> 00:12:36.699
100% of the time.

00:12:36.699 --> 00:12:43.899
But reality is far more nuanced and it will
never ever play out like this.

00:12:43.899 --> 00:12:48.850
At the core of the issue lies the concept
of limited resources.

00:12:48.850 --> 00:12:52.370
Whatever companies are trying to get out of
their customers whether it's money, attention,

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:56.220
or brand loyalty, it’s a finite commodity.

00:12:56.220 --> 00:13:02.090
If every ad becomes impeccable, they all blend
into a sea of perfection, losing the power

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:03.800
to stand out.

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:07.949
The first time that Amazon recommended exactly
what you were looking for, you might’ve

00:13:07.949 --> 00:13:11.300
been impressed and gone ahead and bought the
item right away.

00:13:11.300 --> 00:13:16.690
But what about the second time and the third
time and the thousandth time.

00:13:16.690 --> 00:13:22.139
Nowadays, virtually every ad pertains to something
that you actually want to some degree.

00:13:22.139 --> 00:13:26.269
It’s very rare to get an ad that’s truly
completely irrelevant.

00:13:26.269 --> 00:13:29.220
But do you actually buy from every ad you
see?

00:13:29.220 --> 00:13:31.800
Do you even buy from ads at all?

00:13:31.800 --> 00:13:34.560
I think you can start to see the problem.

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:38.520
When everything is perfect, nothing is.

00:13:38.520 --> 00:13:44.330
Perfection becomes the baseline, and the challenge
lies in exceeding perfection.

00:13:44.330 --> 00:13:46.320
Websites exemplify this phenomenon.

00:13:46.320 --> 00:13:51.460
20 years ago, people were grateful simply
finding a product online, regardless of the

00:13:51.460 --> 00:13:54.320
website's design or minor glitches.

00:13:54.320 --> 00:13:59.180
But today, people wouldn’t consider even
using a website if it doesn’t make a good

00:13:59.180 --> 00:14:03.300
impression within just 0.05 seconds.

00:14:03.300 --> 00:14:07.380
And that’s why you should check out the
sponsor of today’s video Wi…I’m just

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:08.380
kidding.

00:14:08.380 --> 00:14:09.850
We don’t do sponsors on this channel.

00:14:09.850 --> 00:14:12.839
Subscribe if you’d like to continue making
that possible.

00:14:12.839 --> 00:14:18.830
Anyway, while predictive AI undoubtedly provides
a current advantage, it is by no means a gaurantee

00:14:18.830 --> 00:14:20.800
for sustained success.

00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:25.690
People's expectations will continue to escalate,
and the perceived advantage of predictive

00:14:25.690 --> 00:14:39.370
AI will quickly fade away.

00:14:39.370 --> 00:14:43.440
Circling back to the hook of the video, do
I really expect to get a million views on

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:47.070
every video just because creatorml says I
will.

00:14:47.070 --> 00:14:48.579
Of course not.

00:14:48.579 --> 00:14:54.050
For all I know, this video could get just
247 views and then die.

00:14:54.050 --> 00:14:59.199
However, the flip side is equally true as
ignoring the potential of predictive AI is

00:14:59.199 --> 00:15:01.850
a disadvantage in itself.

00:15:01.850 --> 00:15:06.350
Imagine trying to do school today without
Google or code today without Stackoverflow.

00:15:06.350 --> 00:15:10.279
You’d clearly be at a disadvantage compared
to everyone else.

00:15:10.279 --> 00:15:16.170
It’ll be the same case with predictive AI
as well but fortunately, there’s still quite

00:15:16.170 --> 00:15:18.630
some time until that becomes the reality.

00:15:18.630 --> 00:15:24.600
So, be sure to leverage our little secret
before it becomes a daily commodity.

00:15:24.600 --> 00:15:30.230
On YouTube, it seems like AI content has already
become a daily commodity and I think it’s

00:15:30.230 --> 00:15:31.690
very much ruining the platform.

00:15:31.690 --> 00:15:39.749
Check out this video to hear about my thoughts
on AI content farms.

